.1","R.Podgornik.1","M.Bordag.1","Han.Tao.Jing.1","B.Spreng.1","T.Emig.1","F.C.Lombardo.1","L.M.Woods.1","V.M.Mostepanenko.1","G.L.Klimchitskaya.2","D.E.Krause.1","J.Xu.55","Yong.Li.1","T.Tschudi.1","D.A.R.Dalvit.1","S.D.Lopez.1","F.D.Mazzitelli.1","J.Xu.77","V.M.Petrov.2","G.L.Ingold.1","A.W.Rodriguez.1"],"inspire_categories":[{"term":"Condensed Matter","source":"arxiv"},{"term":"Quantum Physics","source":"arxiv"}],"figures":[{"filename":"figRFS-1.png","material":"preprint","caption":"Schematic of the geometrical configuration of MEMS capacitive switch with a cylindrical membrane shown not to scale (see the text for further discussion).","source":"arxiv","label":"fg1","key":"1694e16c4585511e9d9f415374863a07","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/1694e16c4585511e9d9f415374863a07"},{"filename":"figRFS-2.png","material":"preprint","caption":"The dielectric permittivities of Au, Al, and TiO$_2$ are shown as the functions of frequency along the imaginary frequency axis.","source":"arxiv","label":"fg2","key":"e70f6227122fe85e9c0476c8a4833a3e","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/e70f6227122fe85e9c0476c8a4833a3e"},{"filename":"figRFS-3.png","material":"preprint","caption":"The magnitudes of the Casimir and electric forces acting between the smooth surfaces of a membrane and a bottom electrode of the MEMS capacitive switch are shown as the functions of separation by the bottom and top solid lines, respectively. The Casimir force between the membrane and the bottom electrode made of ideal metal is shown by the dashed line.","source":"arxiv","label":"fg3","key":"9559a3969169130bb07a7e1a46ae34e5","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/9559a3969169130bb07a7e1a46ae34e5"},{"filename":"figRFS-4.png","material":"preprint","caption":"The magnitudes of the Casimir and electric forces acting between the rough surfaces of a membrane (roughness model 1) and a bottom electrode of the MEMS capacitive switch are shown as the functions of separation by the bottom and top solid lines, respectively. The bottom and top dashed lines show the same forces acting between smooth surfaces.","source":"arxiv","label":"fg4","key":"6da86b36bed369ab4301e0c2a3c9b383","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/6da86b36bed369ab4301e0c2a3c9b383"},{"filename":"figRFS-5.png","material":"preprint","caption":"The magnitudes of the Casimir and electric forces acting between the rough surfaces of a membrane (roughness models 2, 3, and 1) and a bottom electrode of the MEMS capacitive switch are shown as the functions of separation by the three bottom and two top solid lines, respectively (see the text for further discussion).","source":"arxiv","label":"fg5","key":"b74a66bae2051821e8d4a0ed1e20baad","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/b74a66bae2051821e8d4a0ed1e20baad"}],"preprint_date":"2026-06-26","author_count":4,"first_author":{"full_name":"Klimchitskaya, G.L.","last_name":"Klimchitskaya","first_name":"G.L.","recid":1906968},"public_notes":[{"source":"arXiv","value":"12 pages, 5 figures"}],"control_number":3174267,"dois":[{"material":"publication","source":"arXiv","value":"10.1063/5.0337886"}],"earliest_date":"2026-06-26","document_type":["article"],"texkeys":["Klimchitskaya:2026qva"],"abstracts":[{"source":"arXiv","value":"We determine the role of the fluctuation-induced Casimir force acting between a membrane of cylindrical shape and a bottom electrode in microelectromechanical capacitive switches. For this purpose, the Casimir force is computed taking into account the real properties of both a membrane and a bottom electrode materials with account of surface roughness. The obtained results are compared with those found for the smooth surfaces using the idealization of ideal metal. It is shown that an account of both the real material properties and surface roughness is crucial for obtaining the correct values of the Casimir force. According to our results, at the shortest separations, when the switch membrane is in contact with the transmission line, the magnitudes of the Casimir force may exceed the magnitudes of the electric one depending on the value of the operating voltage. The obtained values of the Casimir force can be used for determining the thickness of the switch membrane, which ensures the necessary magnitude of the restoring elastic force required for a stable cyclic functioning of the micromechanical switch with no pull-in.","abstract_source_suggest":{"input":"arXiv"}}],"primary_arxiv_category":["cond-mat.mes-hall"],"titles":[{"source":"arXiv","title":"Role of the Casimir force in the capacitive radio-frequency microelectromechanical switches"}],"facet_author_name":["1906968_G.L. Klimchitskaya","1990215_V.M. Mostepanenko","2490190_A.V. Loboda","2531515_A.S. Korotkov"],"license":[{"license":"arXiv nonexclusive-distrib 1.0","material":"preprint","url":"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/"}],"_oai":{"sets":["Literature"],"id":"oai:inspirehep.net:3174267","updated":"2026-06-30T04:20:29.579871"},"curated":false,"journal_title_variants":["J.Chem.Phys.","J. Chem. Phys."],"arxiv_eprints":[{"categories":["cond-mat.mes-hall","quant-ph"],"value":"2606.28195"}]},"created":"2026-06-29T04:15:01.571965+00:00","id":"3174267","updated":"2026-06-30T04:20:29.579871+00:00","links":{"bibtex":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/3174267?format=bibtex","latex-eu":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/3174267?format=latex-eu","latex-us":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/3174267?format=latex-us","json":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/3174267?format=json","json-expanded":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/3174267?format=json-expanded","cv":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/3174267?format=cv","citations":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=refersto%3Arecid%3A3174267"}},{"metadata":{"citation_count":1594,"citation_count_without_self_citations":1582,"authors":[{"raw_affiliations":[{"value":"JARA Institute for Quantum Information, RWTH Aachen University, 52056 Aachen, Germany"}],"full_name_unicode_normalized":"terh