edings in Theoretical Computer Science, pages 229–241. Open Publishing Association (2020). https:/​/​doi.org/​10.4204/​EPTCS.318.14"}],"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/2728519"}},{"reference":{"dois":["10.1103/PhysRevX.8.021047"],"label":"46"},"raw_refs":[{"schema":"text","value":"[46] Tomas Jochym-O'Connor, Aleksander Kubica, and Theodore J. Yoder. ``Disjointness of stabilizer codes and limitations on fault-tolerant logical gates''. Phys. Rev. X 8, 021047 (2018). https:/​/​doi.org/​10.1103/​PhysRevX.8.021047"}],"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/2798361"}},{"reference":{"label":"47","publication_info":{"journal_volume":"16","page_end":"953","year":2016,"page_start":"901","journal_title":"Comput."},"misc":["and Peter Selinger. `Òptimal ancilla-free clifford+t approximation of z-rotations''. Quantum Info"],"authors":[{"full_name":"Ross, Neil J."}]},"raw_refs":[{"schema":"text","value":"[47] Neil J. Ross and Peter Selinger. ``Optimal ancilla-free clifford+t approximation of z-rotations''. Quantum Info. Comput. 16, 901–953 (2016)."}]},{"reference":{"dois":["10.1038/s41598-017-10657-8"],"label":"48"},"raw_refs":[{"schema":"text","value":"[48] Alexandru Paler, Simon J Devitt, and Austin G Fowler. ``Synthesis of arbitrary quantum circuits to topological assembly''. Scientific reports 6, 1–16 (2016). https:/​/​doi.org/​10.1038/​s41598-017-10657-8"}],"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/3038936"}},{"reference":{"dois":["10.5281/zenodo.5182845"],"label":"49"},"raw_refs":[{"schema":"text","value":"[49] Cirq Developers. ``Cirq''. Zenodo (2021). https:/​/​doi.org/​10.5281/​zenodo.5182845"}]},{"reference":{"dois":["10.1007/978-3-030-45724-2_10"],"label":"50"},"raw_refs":[{"schema":"text","value":"[50] Samuel Jaques, Michael Naehrig, Martin Roetteler, and Fernando Virdia. ``Implementing grover oracles for quantum key search on aes and lowmc''. In Advances in Cryptology – EUROCRYPT 2020: 39th Annual International Conference on the Theory and Applications of Cryptographic Techniques, Zagreb, Croatia, May 10–14, 2020, Proceedings, Part II. Page 280–310. Berlin, Heidelberg (2020). Springer-Verlag. https:/​/​doi.org/​10.1007/​978-3-030-45724-2_10"}],"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/2747661"}},{"reference":{"dois":["10.1103/PhysRevLett.91.147902"],"label":"51"},"raw_refs":[{"schema":"text","value":"[51] Guifré Vidal. ``Efficient classical simulation of slightly entangled quantum computations''. Phys. Rev. Lett. 91, 147902 (2003). https:/​/​doi.org/​10.1103/​PhysRevLett.91.147902"}],"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/2730432"}},{"reference":{"dois":["10.1007/11535409_1"],"label":"52"},"raw_refs":[{"schema":"text","value":"[52] Bjarne Stroustrup. ``Keynote speech: Abstraction and the c++ machine model''. In Proceedings of the First International Conference on Embedded Software and Systems. Page 1–13. ICESS'04Berlin, Heidelberg (2004). Springer-Verlag. https:/​/​doi.org/​10.1007/​11535409_1"}]},{"reference":{"dois":["10.1038/s41598-017-10657-8"],"label":"53"},"raw_refs":[{"schema":"text","value":"[53] Alexandru Paler, Austin G Fowler, and Robert Wille. ``Synthesis of arbitrary quantum circuits to topological assembly: Systematic, online and compact''. Scientific reports 7, 1–16 (2017). https:/​/​doi.org/​10.1038/​s41598-017-10657-8"}],"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/3038936"}},{"reference":{"dois":["10.1088/1367-2630/aa5709"],"label":"54"},"raw_refs":[{"schema":"text","value":"[54] Daniel Herr, Franco Nori, and Simon J Devitt. ``Lattice surgery translation for quantum computation''. New Journal of Physics 19, 013034 (2017). https:/​/​doi.org/​10.1088/​1367-2630/​aa5709"}],"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/3034666"}},{"reference":{"label":"55","publication_info":{"year":2022},"misc":["JQ-Authors. ``Command-line JSON processor''. https:/​/​github.com/​stedolan/​jq . https:/​/​github.com/​stedolan/​jq"